From e8f144d846ca1e2c84d7784db244e600d802f5a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 01:24:30 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] ui/cocoa: access gl_dirty atomically

drawFrame re-arms gl_dirty from the Cocoa main thread when nextDrawable
returns nil, but the scanout and update callbacks set it and
cocoa_gl_refresh consumes it on the QEMU IO thread.  As a plain bool the
consume can swallow that re-arm, so the dropped present is never retried
and the Metal layer keeps no fresh frame -- the display goes black until
the guest happens to flush again.  A sustained fullscreen guest drops
presents often enough for this to read as a steady flicker.

Consume with qatomic_xchg and set with qatomic_set so a re-arm is never
lost.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
