From fdaf37123a5cf6d74a9da7cd97d1b5b18eadd305 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:29:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] virtio-gpu-gl: initialise the deferred flag on every
 popped command

3bdba2ae2e added virtio_gpu_ctrl_command.deferred and cleared it in
virtio_gpu_handle_ctrl, but the GL device pops commands through
virtio_gpu_gl_handle_ctrl, which never set it.  virtqueue_pop allocates
with g_malloc, so the flag held leftover heap bytes: a command that
landed on a non-zero byte was processed, then taken off cmdq as deferred
and never answered or freed.

The guest sees those as commands that never complete.  On Windows a lost
CREATE_BLOB reply made the KMD retry the id ("resource already exists
25"), and lost unref/fence replies hung shutdown on the "Restarting"
screen (34 unanswered descriptors, empty cmdq and fenceq).  On Linux a
lost context or fence reply stalled Fire Strike and Time Spy at the
second D3D context.

Clear it with the other per-command flags.  Windows install -> reboot ->
desktop: 4/4 pass after, 3/4 failed before.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 hw/display/virtio-gpu-gl.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-gl.c b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-gl.c
index 9f104afa64..29dab4fb7b 100644
--- a/hw/display/virtio-gpu-gl.c
+++ b/hw/display/virtio-gpu-gl.c
@@ -94,6 +94,7 @@ static void virtio_gpu_gl_handle_ctrl(VirtIODevice *vdev, VirtQueue *vq)
         cmd->error = 0;
         cmd->finished = false;
         cmd->suspended = false;
+        cmd->deferred = false;
         QTAILQ_INSERT_TAIL(&g->cmdq, cmd, next);
         cmd = virtqueue_pop(vq, sizeof(struct virtio_gpu_ctrl_command));
     }
-- 
