From 88e5ee7ec6703662fec7b638cca74c4769e683d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: osy <osy@turing.llc>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:42:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-gpu: initialise popped control commands in one helper

virtio_gpu_process_cmdq() reads cmd->suspended and cmd->deferred for every
device, but each handle_ctrl loop reset the per-command state on its own.
fdaf37123a fixed the GL loop for deferred; the rutabaga loop still set only
vq, error and finished, so its commands carried leftover g_malloc bytes in
both flags and could be parked at the queue head or dropped without a
response.

Move the reset into virtio_gpu_ctrl_cmd_init() and call it from all three
loops, so a new per-command flag is initialised in one place.

